| 4 | 2 | even | 2 → impossible ($4{\times}1\neq 6$); 4 → all $\binom{4}{3}{=}4$ triples, each elt in 3 | ✓ | **4** |
| 5 | 2 | odd | 3 → $a{=}2$: $\{a,b,c_1\},\{a,b,c_2\},\{a,b,c_3\}$ | ✓ | **3** |
